## Generic Axis Lengths

Slices are used to define generic functions that manipulate arrays with any number of axes of any lengths.

For example: 
```
func add[Shape int](float32, [unpack(Shape)]float32) [unpack(Shape)]float32
```
defines an `add` function with one generic argument, `Shape` of type `[]int`, and which takes two non-generic (runtime) arguments: a `float32` scalar, and an array of `float32` with any number of axes. `add` returns an array with the same shape. 

We use the `unpack` builtin function to transform the slice `Shape` into the axis lengths of an array. (This syntax is temporary and will probably be replaced with `Shape...` instead).

The `add` function can then be called with different array shapes as in the example.
